; walk-skip-end — `+++` is skipped and `---` ends the song.
;
; Orders [0, +++, 1, ---, 2]: the `+++` plays nothing and the walk moves
; on, the `---` is where the song ends and loops back to order 0, and the
; order after it never plays. (The canonical writer appends its own
; trailing `---`, so the file carries six orders where the module had
; five; neither marker is reached twice.)
;
; The fixture's patterns are shorter than IT 2.14's floor of 32 rows, so
; the reader warns once per pattern and honours them — which is what puts
; this row map beside plan 06's hand computation instead of beside a
; padded one.
(read)
(walk)
